# Māori Biomimetic Symbiotic Chassis: Technical Architecture

**The `MāoriSymbioticSuit` engine maps the structural geometries of Whakairo (Carving), Kōwhaiwhai (Fluid Scroll Work), and Tukutuku (Lattice Weaving) into adaptive biomimetic sub-systems.** This translation bridges traditional visual languages with structural engineering to manage closed-loop oxygen supply, ballistic deflection, life support, and hazardous environment seals.

---

## 1. Functional Mapping Matrix

| Operational Theatre | Traditional Art Geometry | Biomimetic Translation | Primary Technical Function |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Aeronautical Infiltration** | *Pūhoro Tika* & *Pītau Takarangi* | Parallel tracking vectors & pierced open-work spirals | Sequences fluid currents across limbs, manages frictionless thermal exhaust expansion, and eliminates boundary-layer wake drag. |
| **High-Impact Land Combat** | *Tuara-Kurī Tika* & *Pātiki Paparua* | Symmetrical herringbone spines & nested diamond chest plating | Distributes extreme vertical landing forces across the lower chassis and fractures head-on kinetic concussions. |
| **Subsurface Amphibious** | *Unaunahi Takitahi* & *Marakihau* | Isolated crescent indentations & hollow tubular siphons | Mimics micro-skin textures to shed water drag and processes currents through internal conversion loops for thermal ballast. |
| **Chemical & CBRN Defense** | *Manaia Hiku-Peke* & *Kaokao Tārua* | Coiled profile perimeters & interlocking double-chevrons | Establishes an impenetrable, gas-tight hermetic seal across chassis joints that maintains isolation during deep respiration cycles. |
| **Life Support / Closed-Loop Oxygen** | *Koiri Mangōpare* & *Koru Whakakahu* | Branching neural channels & nested scroll pathways | Monitors host biometrics to dynamically regulate internal atmospheres and automatically routes active biopolymer resins to self-heal breaches. |

